From 0853f027b0cfc61e9393f32ee220d3eced2e0def Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fangjian Ju <roger@FangjiandeMacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:00:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [rh2-integration] leaf identity on the train wire + per-rank
 step facts + engine-actor identity

Pre-rental focused-fix batch (rh2 miles GPU spike G1 acceptance):

1. Unique fan-out leaf identity (rh2 #1): fan-out sibling Samples inherit one
   agent run's Sample.index, so sample_indices alone cannot tell two
   legitimate leaves apart nor bind a per-leaf routing tape to the right
   leaf. Add the thin pair (sample_index, leaf_ordinal):
   - train_data_conversion: compute_leaf_ordinals() (occurrence index per
     run key = rollout_id falling back to index, over the flattened sample
     order) + new 'leaf_ordinals' rollout_data column (VALUE_SPEC + dp-shard
     split list). rollout_ids/group_index grouping semantics untouched.
   - rollout_manager._emit_rollout_evidence: rollout_group events carry
     leaf_ordinals computed with the same function over the same order.
   - megatron model.py: get_batch forwards leaf_ordinals; train_step_consumed
     events carry per-position leaf_ordinals.
   - megatron actor.py: replay_fill events carry sample_indices +
     leaf_ordinals row-aligned with sample_digests (leaf_id -> digest exact
     linkage instead of digest multisets); logprob_compare entries carry
     leaf_ordinal (miles/utils/logprob_compare.py, optional column).

2. Per-rank step oracle input (rh2 #2): train_step events carry
   num_rollouts (the exact opt_param_scheduler.step increment), so the
   acceptance judge can require scheduler_steps_after == before +
   num_rollouts per rank instead of 'advanced by something'.

3. SGLang identity under broadcast (rh2 #3): SGLangEngine.init() asserts and
   emits the 'sglang_engine' integration-tree identity before the transfer-
   mode dispatch -- the actor exists under both broadcast and RDT, while
   SGLangServerActor ('sglang_server', kept) only exists on the RDT branch,
   so a server-actor-only identity is deterministically absent on broadcast
   runs. No transfer-mode change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
